WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.950
Here's the heart of the
gate: the earliest end.

2
00:00:02.950 --> 00:00:06.375
A contractor can stop needing
access for several reasons,

3
00:00:06.375 --> 00:00:08.088
and the rules file lists them.

4
00:00:08.088 --> 00:00:09.563
The contract ends.

5
00:00:09.563 --> 00:00:12.712
The completion date comes
earlier than the contract end.

6
00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:14.675
Suitability is withdrawn.

7
00:00:14.675 --> 00:00:17.875
The card is terminated,
revoked or expired.

8
00:00:17.875 --> 00:00:22.850
The sponsor separates, plus a grace
period, thirty days in the program's file.

9
00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:27.800
Or the sponsor misses a recertification,
every hundred eighty days in the file.

10
00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:30.812
The extract computes every
condition that applies

11
00:00:30.812 --> 00:00:33.263
to each contractor and
takes the first one.

12
00:00:33.263 --> 00:00:36.776
That's the earliest end, and
it becomes the leave date.

13
00:00:36.776 --> 00:00:41.080
A missing contract end isn't treated
as no end; the record doesn't go

14
00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:45.625
through at all, because a contractor
is never provisioned open-ended.

15
00:00:45.625 --> 00:00:50.980
The grace and recertification periods are
design guidance: your agency sets them.
